  message: "STILL OPEN — verified NOT a pure F1 (envelope) duplicate; it tracks a distinct, currently-UNMET flag-SPELLING-uniformity gap. Flag audit (.ci/cli-flag-matrix.json @ dev 24b44a1d0d): --format json on 6 read subcommands (cache-status, catalog, config, dead-code-maybe, routes, test-coverage) but --json still on io-boundaries + verify-claims; slice uses --flat (orthogonal payload-shape axis, not a format selector). INV-fivar (sub-A, satisfied) only retrofitted --format json onto the flag-LESS trio (cache-status/catalog/routes via add_schema_envelope); it did NOT touch the pre-existing --json subcommands, so the 'same spelling everywhere' invariant is unmet. Remaining work to close: add --format {text,json} to io-boundaries + verify-claims (keep --json as a hidden back-compat alias mapping to format=json), bringing every JSON-emitting read subcommand to one spelling; regen cli-flag-matrix + update help/spec/changelog. This is the last gap blocking WI-gogif's 'one consistent convention' expectation."  # c657
