  message: "DONE — PR #537 (selfh/dev 4d933c251f). io-boundaries + verify-claims now expose the canonical --format {text,json} (default text) via a shared _read_view_wants_json(args) helper; --json kept as a back-compat alias (--json wins when both given). All 8 text-defaulting read views (cache-status/catalog/config/dead-code-maybe/routes/test-coverage + io-boundaries/verify-claims) share one flag spelling. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (live @ dev 4d933c251f, /tmp fixture os.listdir+subprocess.run): 'io-boundaries --format json' -> parseable JSON (total_io_edges=2, boundaries=[fs_read,subprocess]); '--json' alias -> identical JSON; '--format text' -> 'I/O Boundary Map (2 boundary calls)'. 'verify-claims --claims ... --format json' -> parseable JSON (view=verify-claims, schema_version=1.0, 1 verdict); '--json' alias -> identical; '--format text' -> 'checkmark [SC-001] ... Verdict: confirmed'. Both --help list '--format {text,json}' (canonical) + '--json' (alias). Wire envelopes byte-identical (IO_BOUNDARIES/VERIFY_CLAIMS schema_versions unchanged); additive flag, no schema bump; flag-matrix regenerated; core 100% coverage. slice/compact excluded (JSON-only category, no text mode). Closes the last flag-spelling gap under WI-gogif."  # 2d15
